findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test or code distinguishes NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    The config loading tests don't cover permission/parse error scenarios being swallowed.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #1 flagged CWE-209 risk in ServerError Display impl,
    noting the inner string is dead data and changing format to include {0} would
    leak server internals. TEA also wrote CWE-209 tests in exit_codes.rs, but reviewer
    provided the specific structural analysis.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in siem_client.rs covering CRLF rejection\
    \ in token/tenant values. Dev implemented explicit \\n/\\r checks in client.rs:19-23,31-35.\
    \ However, the deeper issue of using raw String instead of validated TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core was not flagged \u2014 only the injection vector was partially\
    \ mitigated."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #5: ''clap_complete not declared as workspace dependency''
    and ''Same for comfy-table, keyring, dirs, csv, toml. This violates the workspace
    dependency management pattern.'' Listed as HIGH and required before approval.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig (config.rs:8),
    verified by reviewer finding #20. This causes unknown fields like token to error
    rather than be silently ignored. Reviewer finding #15 noted the defense works
    but by coincidence.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #11: 'config_handles_unknown_fields_gracefully test\
    \ has vacuous assertion \u2014 assert!(config.is_ok() || config.is_err()) \u2014\
    \ This assertion is always true.' Listed as MEDIUM and required fix before approval."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #12: 'exit_code_success_is_zero test is vacuous \u2014\
    \ assert_eq!(0i32, 0) \u2014 This asserts a literal equals itself. It doesn't\
    \ test any code.' Also finding #13 flagged another vacuous assertion. Required\
    \ fix before approval."
